    subtract_s1_text: "Barsik will show you the opposite trick! Subtraction is when part of the objects go away, and we count how many are left. Ready to try?",
    subtract_s2_title: "Addition and Subtraction — Opposite Friends",
    subtract_s2_text: "Addition combines two groups, while subtraction, on the other hand, removes part of the objects. One is the opposite of the other.",
    subtract_s3_title: "Example: Birds Fly Away",
    subtract_s3_text: "5 birds were sitting on a branch. 2 birds flew away. We count: 5 − 2 = 3. 3 birds are left.",
    subtract_s4_title: "The Minus Sign",
    subtract_s4_text: "The \"−\" sign means subtraction. When you see it between numbers, count how many are left after part of the objects go away.",
    subtract_s5_title: "Another Example",
    subtract_s5_text: "There were 8 balloons, 3 popped. 8 − 3 = 5. 5 balloons are left.",
    subtract_s6_title: "You Can Subtract!",
