  "hub_bodyhealth_desc": "Squelette, muscles, hygiène",
  "est2air_explain": "Barsik will tell you about air! Air is all around us and every living thing needs it to breathe. It is clear, has no colour or smell, and fills all the free space. Find the right picture, sort things into baskets and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2air_game_title": "Air Around Us",
  "est2air_game_sub": "What do you know about air?",
  "hub_est2air_title": "L'air",
  "hub_est2air_desc": "Respiration, vent, propriétés de l'air",
  "est2resources_explain": "Barsik will tell you about natural resources! Everything people take from nature to live is called natural resources: water, air, soil, forest, coal, oil. Some resources come from living nature and some from non-living nature. Find the right picture, sort the resources and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2resources_game_title": "Natural Resources",
  "est2resources_game_sub": "What does nature give us?",
  "hub_est2resources_title": "Ressources naturelles",
  "hub_est2resources_desc": "Eau, air, sol, charbon, forêt",
  "est2earthsun_explain": "Barsik will tell you about the Earth, the Sun and the Moon! The Sun is a star and gives the Earth light and warmth. The Earth is our planet. The Moon is the natural satellite of the Earth: it moves around it. Find the right picture, sort the space bodies and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2earthsun_game_title": "Earth, Sun and Moon",
  "est2earthsun_game_sub": "How are they connected?",
  "hub_est2earthsun_title": "La Terre, le Soleil et la Lune",
  "hub_est2earthsun_desc": "Lumière et chaleur, satellite naturel",
  "est2planets_explain": "Barsik will tell you about the planets! Eight planets move around the Sun: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune. They differ in size and in distance from the Sun. Find the right picture, sort the planets and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2planets_game_title": "Planets of the Solar System",
  "est2planets_game_sub": "Which planet is which?",
  "hub_est2planets_title": "Les planètes",
  "hub_est2planets_desc": "Ordre des planètes et comparaison",
  "est2timeunits_explain": "Barsik will tell you about time! Time is measured in seconds, minutes, hours, days, weeks, months and years. In space the distances are so huge that it takes a very long time to reach the stars. Find the right picture, sort the units of time and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2timeunits_game_title": "Units of Time",
  "est2timeunits_game_sub": "How do we measure time?",
  "hub_est2timeunits_title": "Temps et distances",
  "hub_est2timeunits_desc": "Seconde, minute, heure, jour, année",
  "est2speed_explain": "Barsik will tell you about movement! Some bodies move fast and some move slowly. A body starts to move when it is pushed or pulled: forces are acting. The mass of a body is measured with scales. Find the right picture, sort the bodies and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2speed_game_title": "Fast and Slow",
  "est2speed_game_sub": "How does each thing move?",
  "hub_est2speed_title": "Vite et lentement",
  "hub_est2speed_desc": "Vitesse du mouvement, forces, masse",
  "est2lightpass_explain": "Barsik will tell you about light! Some bodies let light through well — they are transparent, like glass and clean water. Others let a little light through — they are translucent, like tracing paper. Opaque bodies do not let light through at all: brick, wood, metal. Find the right picture, sort the bodies and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2lightpass_game_title": "What Lets Light Through?",
  "est2lightpass_game_sub": "Transparent and opaque bodies",
  "hub_est2lightpass_title": "Lumière et transparence",
  "hub_est2lightpass_desc": "Corps transparents, translucides et opaques",
  "est2soundloud_explain": "Barsik will tell you about sounds! Sounds can be loud or quiet. Very loud sounds are bad for hearing, so we must look after our ears. Sources of sound can be sorted by loudness: a whisper is quiet and a drum is loud. Find the right picture, sort the sources of sound and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
  "est2soundloud_game_title": "Loud and Quiet Sounds",
  "est2soundloud_game_sub": "Which sound is louder?",
  "hub_est2soundloud_title": "Volume du son",
  "hub_est2soundloud_desc": "Sources de son selon le volume",
  "est2temperature_explain": "Barsik will tell you about temperature! Temperature shows how warm or cold a body is. It is measured with a thermometer and the unit is the degree Celsius. The hotter a body is, the higher its temperature. Find the right picture, sort the bodies and answer \"true\" or \"false\". Ready?",
